    "finding": "Pinning itself does not cause the extra round. The batch's third call was forced by a group-baseline false positive whose payload was byte-identical before and after, and the largest payload the plugin ever sent (10,382 bytes) is 6.3x below the frozen 65,216-byte ceiling, so pinning never pushed the payload over a limit and never triggered a budget fallback. The v3/v4 history shows the extra round appears whenever an elision makes the model re-issue a tool (v3 = 3 calls, v4 = 2 calls with the largest text deleted); v5 removed the elision of the constraint carrier but still elided read_django_count_entry, so the round structure stayed at 3. The recorded evidence cannot prove which of those drove the model's decision on any single sample, and this diagnosis does not claim it can.",
